--- ADDED (this project's contribution — see docs/DESIGN.md) ---------------

Auto-annotation pipeline (Rust):

A   src-tauri/src/reconstruction/colmap.rs
        COLMAP sparse-reconstruction reader (cameras.bin / images.bin /
        points3D.bin) and camera projection mathematics, with unit tests
        that verify the binary layout by round-trip against synthetic files.
A   src-tauri/src/reconstruction/inspect.rs
        Project audit: frame counts, camera registration ratio, camera
        intrinsics, sparse point statistics, and a readiness check that
        decides whether a reconstruction can be used for auto-annotation.
A   src-tauri/src/reconstruction/autolabel.rs
        3D bounding-box fitting from the sparse point cloud (with the up
        axis inferred from the camera trajectory), projection of that box
        into every registered frame, per-frame quality checks, YOLO label
        export, CSV/JSON reports and a dependency-free HTML review sheet.
A   src-tauri/src/reconstruction/cloud.rs
        Sparse point-cloud loading for the in-app live reconstruction
        viewer, preferring intermediate snapshots and falling back to the
        published model.
A   src-tauri/src/pipeline/monitor.rs
        Live monitoring of the reconstruction stage feeding the point-cloud
        viewer.

Frontend (added):

A   src/components/PointCloud/PointCloudViewer.tsx
A   src/components/PointCloud/projection.ts
A   src/components/PointCloud/projection.test.ts
A   src/components/PointCloud/index.ts
        In-app live 3D point-cloud view reached from the mapping stage,
        with its own projection tests.

Documentation and compliance (added):

A   docs/DESIGN.md
        Design rationale for the post-reconstruction annotation stage.
A   docs/COMPLIANCE.md
        Licensing, originality, and competition disclosure statement.

Build, packaging, and CI (added):

A   scripts/stage-cli.mjs
        Stages the splatstudio CLI into Tauri's bundle.externalBin location,
        which is required before any `tauri build`.
A   scripts/join-installer-parts.ps1
        Reassembles and SHA-256-verifies the chunked Windows installer.

See "MODIFIED (build, packaging, and CI)" below for the workflow files and
the other scripts that changed as part of this work.

